# Seiche's speed dial (physics catalog plan, 2026-10-03): fast-forward under
# the frame budget, half of each measured frame by default (ruled 2026-10-04,
# "Target + Max, budget as frame share").
# tree.html?nodes=300&seed=7&links=none&gpu=off&physics_speed=max runs as fast
# as the budget allows, so the budget binds every frame, the canvas reports
# the speed it reached, and stepping stays inside each frame's own budget.
# (At 50x the budget, half of this page's slowed frame, outgrows the catch-up
# cap, which binds first.) p6_tree_speed_fast_control is 50x at 24 nodes.
assert snap ready == true
assert snap physics-speed == max
assert snap physics-budget-share == 0.5
click role:button Play physics
settle 2
assert snap physics-paused == false
click role:combobox Arrangement
settle 1
click role:option Free (physics alone)
settle 1
click role:button Apply arrangement
settle 1
assert snap layout == free
settle 10
timing start speed-fast
settle 30
timing stop
log-physics fast
assert snap physics-budget-bound == true
assert snap physics-effective-speed >= 1
assert snap pace-frames == 30
# Each frame's bound is its budget, the share of the measured frame, plus
# the browser clock's 100 us resolution (performance.now), ruled 2026-10-04,
# "Bound = budget + clock grain", carried to the frame-share budget.
assert snap pace-over-budget-us <= 100
assert snap finite == true
log p6 speed fast receipt complete
